WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.340
Daddy! Mommy!

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.310
Ellie!

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.900
Thank god...

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.680
Isn't this great, Ellie?

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.680
Thank you, Mister!

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.690
Well, you know...

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.690
Just doin' my job!

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.950
I even got paid up front, so...

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.360
Thank you very much!

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.030
It's over.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.700
Yup.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.370
How big you've grown, Ellie!

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.930
Having a family... is nice.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:54.380
<i>That's how it always starts...</i>
<i>under the azure sky</i>

00:00:54.380 --> 00:01:01.290
<i>After making a vow,</i>
<i>I now set off</i>

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>Yeah, the desert glitters with a golden hue</i>
<i>(The wind is scorching)</i>

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:27.020
<i>I'm searching for a diamond flower</i>
<i>(I keep on wandering)</i>

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:33.350
<i>Now, for the first time in my life,</i>

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:39.690
<i>I live for someone else</i>

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:46.200
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I wanna protect</i>

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:52.210
<i>I'll never,</i>
<i>ever lose it again</i>

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:55.710
<i>Resound,</i>
<i>my heartbeat!</i>

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:05.710
<i>A heartbeat smaller and fragile,</i>
<i>but tougher than anyone's.</i>

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:22.260
"Drowning Cat"

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.680
Hm? What is this?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.910
Eden Project?

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.010
Not found? The data must've been deleted.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:47.520
If their data admin is clueless,
I just may be able to recover it.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.970
There! Yes!

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.640
This is!

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.980
"Due to the collapse of Bioberg,
the project was cancelled?

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.980
This was not an accident,
but a terrorist act.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.320
The research facility was totally destroyed,

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:15.320
and the prototype machines
under development were also stolen.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:19.660
Torneo Rudman, the perpetrator,
was killed at the hands of Chronos;

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:23.000
however, the whereabouts of the
prototype machines are still unknown.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:28.570
The chief researcher of the Eden Project,
Dr. Tearju Lunatique,

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.000
was also critically injured
and is currently hospitalized."

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.340
Which hospital?

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.540
You need a password!?

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.180
How about... femalescientist!

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:47.020
Damn! They must've waited until
the Numbers were gone to attack.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.510
Contact Sephiria-<i>sama</i> immediately!

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.640
What the!?

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.600
What's going on!?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:09.010
It doesn't seem as though

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:12.650
you've taken those from the
Apostles of the Stars as prisoners.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:16.650
How pitiful... you seem quite confused.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:22.660
You are Numbers! Are you telling us
you were conspiring with the enemy!?

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.320
You still don't get it?

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.990
The days of Chronos are over.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:30.660
Now we, the Zero Numbers, will take over.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.670
Zero Numbers!?

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:36.800
It seems that this was planned
from the very beginning... Mason!

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.680
Mason! You are a serious threat
to the noble cause of Chronos.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.340
And I shall erase you!

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.680
You're not in any position
to be talking tough!

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.680
You simply cannot see beyond
Chronos' way of thinking, can you?

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.020
We do have our own noble cause, as well.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.020
Sephiria...

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:59.360
I have waited a long time for this day...

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.130
the day that we take a step
towards ultimate peace.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.100
This is farewell!

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.310
Hey Bro!

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.650
Bro! I'm glad you're back safe!

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:23.980
Yo!

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.510
H- hey!

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:35.160
Bro!

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.690
--Cheers!
--Cheers!
--Cheers!

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.000
Bro! Congratulations on your
attaining your long-cherished goal!

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.670
I'm so relieved!

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.070
Well, I knew you'd be back safe,

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.340
but considering the enemy
you were up against...

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:52.010
If anything had happened to you...
I was just so worried!

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:54.350
Err... Hey Bro, are you listening?

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.680
More milk, please!

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.020
Geez! C'mon, Bro!

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.290
Ah... ah... Ah-choo!

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.290
Hey, quit spitting all over the place!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.290
S- sorry.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.390
Here's your milk.

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:14.630
Annette!? What're you doing here!?

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:19.970
Woodney told me... that you
took on some dangerous job...

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:24.640
So I brought all sorts of things.
I guess it was for nothing.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.980
We don't need any of that stuff.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:29.650
Humph! As cocky as ever!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.650
I'm surprised you were
able to procure the boat.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:36.760
The fishermen in this area were
too afraid of the Apostles of the Stars

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.320
to take their boats out.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.330
I hired a boatman
who cared little about life.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.000
It cost me a fortune, though.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.670
When you collect your bounty,
I expect a big cut.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.000
There won't be any bounty this time.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.340
What do you mean?

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.340
Err... Haven't a clue...

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.340
Don't tell me you let Creed escape!?

00:06:55.340 --> 00:07:00.010
Don't worry! We crushed
the Apostles of the Stars good.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:02.950
You beat the Apostles of the Stars,
yet you get no reward!?

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.620
What's the meaning of this?

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.290
Aw c'mon... let it go.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:10.620
The Sweeper Association guys
are okay with it, too, so...

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:14.290
Right? You guys don't care
about the reward, right?

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:19.300
Err... you do, huh?

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.970
Sure you do. Even I do...

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.060
I don't care.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:30.310
We didn't lose to even
the Apostles of the Stars.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:33.980
No matter what kind of job we take
from now on, we're sure to succeed.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:35.610
Eve...

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.320
She's right!

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:43.990
In any event, with this battle,
we Sweepers proved ourselves as men!

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:45.990
And as women, too!

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:49.660
Right! We beat those monsters!

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.000
The bounty means nothing!

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.670
--Right! Right!
--Right! Right!
--Right! Right!

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:59.670
I'm impressed! You first-class sweepers
really are different from the rest!

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.410
Tonight's on me! Drink all you like!

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:05.500
--Alright!
--Alright!
--Alright!

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.620
They're all gone.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:21.960
They went off to their next jobs.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.330
Being a sweeper isn't a stable job...

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:27.300
you follow where the wind
and criminals take you.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.630
I see...

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:34.600
Let's head out to our next job, too.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.310
Say Eve... what do you
want to do from now on?

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:40.980
What?

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:45.320
You can't keep roaming
around with us, right?

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:48.320
The Apostles of the Stars
have been destroyed.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.320
Why not attend school or something?

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:55.990
Like that fire-breathing girl, Kyoko.
Attend a school in Zipang or something.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:58.000
Since Zipang is a safe country,
it'd probably be-

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.930
I like just how it is.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.730
I want to live freely.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.940
You know, I'm saying this for you.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.950
You should get into a
prestigious girls' boarding school

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:17.950
and get some education
under a respectable teacher.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:21.290
If you're worried about the tuition,
I'll find a way to...

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.220
Hey, where are you going!?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.630
Sven... you don't understand anything.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.060
Eve!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:34.230
Geez... they don't even have a
milk vending machine in this town!?

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:40.310
Something wrong with the princess?

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:41.740
It's nothing.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.780
Miss Eve?

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.690
It's been a long time, Eve.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:29.020
I wonder if you've forgotten...

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:32.690
that we're very old friends.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.360
Friends?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:39.700
Yes, I was there when you were born.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:44.360
Come, Eve. I'll take you to paradise.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:33.410
What in the!?

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:46.370
Since you're here, there must be
no mistake that this is the gathering place.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:48.700
Number VII!

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.370
Where are the others?

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:53.370
I can't find them anywhere...

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.040
I found David's body.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.040
I've just buried him.

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:02.650
Then could Sephiria-<i>san</i>
and Belze-<i>san</i> also be...

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.320
There's no way those two
would be defeated.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.410
I'm sure they're out searching
for Baldor and the others.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.670
That's...

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.670
Sephiria-<i>san</i>!

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.000
Belze-<i>san</i>!

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.770
Anubis!

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:33.680
No good!

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:36.680
This one doesn't work either!

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.510
Nor this...

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.950
Just as expected, this is impossible!

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:46.020
I'm so exhausted!

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:48.690
I'm sleepy... my shoulders are aching...

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:50.920
My butt hurts, too...

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:57.370
Ahh! I'm starving!

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:02.310
Even a simple omelet will do. I wanna eat!

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.710
Omelet!?

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:13.320
<i>The disk was empty, but I kept it</i>
<i>because of the weird title...</i>

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:17.850
<i>"Tips on how to make rolled omelets</i>
<i>without turning them into toxic waste."</i>

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:29.670
Thank you for coming, but Ms. Lunatique
may not recognize you as her cousin.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:34.340
The shock of the accident at Bioberg
has caused her to lose her memory.

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:36.210
This way.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.350
Oh? She's not here.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:45.350
Strange... she should be
done with her rehab session,

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.410
and I don't think any tests
were scheduled on her today.

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:52.690
What was that?

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:56.700
Someone, help! The patient in 303 is...

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.670
She's agitated again after
seeing herself in the mirror!

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:25.990
You actually said that to the child?

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:27.290
Poor thing!

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:30.000
--Saying that to her after
she trusted you so much...
--Refill, please!

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.670
Precisely because I'm close to her,
I'm thinking about Eve's future, and...

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:38.340
Sven! You always
call yourself a gentleman...

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.670
but you're such a coward, aren't you!?

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.340
What!?

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:46.010
It seems to me that you're
trying to run away from Eve.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:49.350
Hey! More milk, please!

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:53.020
You said, "Eve is not some sort of weapon.
She's a human being."

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:55.450
Then, isn't it important
not just to protect her,

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.790
but to think about her feelings as well!?

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:03.300
Let's go.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.960
Let's go and get the princess.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.300
She's probably sulking somewhere...

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.640
thinking, "Why isn't Sven
coming to get me already?"

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.100
C'mon, let's go.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.310
The adjustments to the improved
NS amplifier have been completed.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.040
Aside from the transformation control,

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.980
access permissions to the apperception
system have also been registered.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:25.320
So, it won't accept
any input from anyone but us.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:29.590
Furthermore, the pick-up rate
of all the data

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.320
that Eve has stored in her memory
and emotion filters have been optimized.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:37.330
At this point, there is nothing
in the way of activating Eden.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.000
Good.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:44.000
Eve... How long I've waited
to see you again...

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:49.670
From the very day when Dr. Lunatique
created you at Bioberg.

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:52.680
You will now proceed to paradise...

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:57.640
to Eden... where it will all begin.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:06.290
Eve! Where are you!?

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:08.290
Come on home now!

00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:12.630
Let's go get something good to eat!

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:15.970
Hey Train! What're you doing up there?

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:19.640
Huh? Of course I'm looking
for the princess!

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:22.310
I know! I'm asking why you're on the roof!

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:25.980
When people are lonely,
they like to climb up to high places.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:27.650
That's common sense.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:30.980
She's not you! You won't
find her up on a roof!

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:32.650
Get serious and look!

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:35.650
Mister Sven!

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.660
Ellie...

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.990
What're you doing here?
Did you come to see the boats?

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:44.900
No. But what are you doing out so late?

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:48.330
I came to greet Daddy.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.670
Oh? You did? Good girl.

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:54.010
Oh! Good evening!

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:56.010
H- hello...

00:16:56.010 --> 00:17:00.010
Say Ellie, Eve still hasn't come back.

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.280
Did you see her somewhere?

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:04.280
Miss Eve?

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:07.620
Oh, that blonde child?
I saw her at the harbor.

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:08.620
Really?

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:12.960
Yes. A man who looks like a doctor
in a white lab coat was with her.

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.630
A doctor!? When!?

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:19.300
I went back and forth between the harbor
and my house several times today,

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.630
but I think it was in the morning.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.540
Do you know which way they went?

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:38.320
We were finally able to obtain Eve.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:41.990
The realization of
the ideal world is near!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:46.320
I am grateful for all your work.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:50.760
To think that a young girl like this...
has the power to change the world...

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:03.610
Eve!!

00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:06.840
Where are you!? Eve!!

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:15.290
Eve! So, that's where you were!

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:18.620
Let's go home, Eve.

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:22.290
Say, let's talk things over.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.850
Hey, you can stop fooling around now.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.690
Th- that's...

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:35.970
Eve says she's not going back to you.

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.980
Quit talking nonsense!

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.650
You're making her say that!

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:41.980
Wait right there, Eve!

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:47.650
I'll free you... right away!

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:56.390
Sven!

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:10.470
Hah! It's been a long time, Black Cat.

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.820
Since when did Chrono Numbers

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:19.950
start hiring the Apostles of the Stars
to abduct people?

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:22.950
We are no longer Chronos.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:26.290
We are comrades.

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:29.630
I don't give a damn who you team up with!!

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:31.630
Give Eve back now!!

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:34.300
Unfortunately, we can't.

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:39.300
We have a far deeper bond with Eve.

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.310
What!?

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:44.310
We know everything there is
to know about Eve.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:47.650
Shut up!! What do you know about Eve!?

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:50.980
Scum like you couldn't possibly
understand how she feels!

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:52.980
Hah! How she feels?

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:55.020
Even if people understand
each other's feelings,

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:57.660
it does not stop them from fighting.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.320
Mason!

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:01.990
So you're the mastermind behind all this!

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:05.330
Chronos once tried to destroy Eve.

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:08.670
So why do you want her now?

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:13.340
For the magnificent
and noble plan, Black Cat.

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:16.340
I am grateful to you both, though...

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:20.680
for nurturing Eve to this point.

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:25.350
Now, we will be able to change the world.

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:27.690
I don't know what the hell
you're talking about!

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:29.350
Just what does that have to do with Eve!?

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:31.790
Come, Eve.

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:35.880
Eve!?

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:43.300
It's time to bid farewell.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.660
Eve!!

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.320
Sven!

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.660
Wait!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.250
Eve!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.730
Sven!

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:43.460
Eve...

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:53.370
Eve, this is Eden.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:54.710
Eden...

00:21:54.710 --> 00:22:00.310
Now go... Adam is waiting for you.

00:22:00.310 --> 00:22:02.080
Adam...

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:21.330
<i>Since your new black boots</i>
<i>caused a blister,</i>

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:28.340
<i>you rest your right foot</i>

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:38.340
<i>We'll keep walking along</i>
<i>with our own rhythm, without rushing</i>

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:51.850
<i>Don't say anything</i>
<i>because we'll soon understand each other</i>

00:22:56.400 --> 00:23:06.400
<i>I'm just holding you now to keep you warm</i>

00:23:10.650 --> 00:23:20.650
<i>I'm completely wrapped around you, so...</i>

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:31.060
<i>Quietly the powder-like snow</i>
<i>is building up...</i>

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:41.340
"Next Episode"

00:23:41.340 --> 00:23:43.410
<i>Eve, I have waited so long for your return.</i>
"Next Episode"

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:45.350
<i>Eve, I have waited so long for your return.</i>

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:48.350
<i>Now my plan will be fulfilled.</i>

00:23:48.350 --> 00:23:54.360
<i>Look, this is Eden, the salvation</i>
<i>that mankind has long awaited.</i>

00:23:54.360 --> 00:24:00.960
<i>Eve, from now on, you and Eden</i>
<i>will bring ultimate peace to mankind.</i>

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:02.430
<i>It is splendid... too splendid!</i>

00:24:02.430 --> 00:24:05.400
"Cat Sharpens His Claws"
<i>It is splendid... too splendid!</i>
